#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build and run a Qiskit Function template for electronic structure simulation"
" with an implicit solvent model {#build-and-run-a-qiskit-function-template-"
"for-electronic-structure-simulation-with-an-implicit-solvent-model}"
msgstr ""
"Bumuo at patakbuhin ang isang Qiskit Function template para sa electronic "
"structure simulation na may implicit solvent model {#build-and-run-a-qiskit-"
"function-template-for-electronic-structure-simulation-with-an-implicit-"
"solvent-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore pvdz, fcisolver, avas, ncas, nelecas, ecore, chkfile, "
"fcivec, hcore, ncore, myci, sqdvec, myeps, mymethod, mysolvmethod, myavas, "
"mcscf, MCSCF, chkfile, prqs */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore pvdz, fcisolver, avas, ncas, nelecas, ecore, chkfile, "
"fcivec, hcore, ncore, myci, sqdvec, myeps, mymethod, mysolvmethod, myavas, "
"mcscf, MCSCF, chkfile, prqs */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This template, developed in collaboration with the Cleveland Clinic, "
"consists of a workflow to calculate the ground state energy and solvation "
"free energy of a molecule in an implicit solvent [[1]](#references). These "
"simulations are based on the sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) "
"method [[2-6]](#references) and the integral equation formalism polarizable "
"continuum model (IEF-PCM) of solvent [[7]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang template na ito, na binuo sa pakikipagtulungan sa Cleveland Clinic, ay "
"binubuo ng isang workflow para kalkulahin ang ground state energy at "
"solvation free energy ng isang molecule sa isang implicit solvent "
"[[1]](#references). Ang mga simulation na ito ay batay sa sample-based "
"quantum diagonalization (SQD) method [[2-6]](#references) at ang integral "
"equation formalism polarizable continuum model (IEF-PCM) ng solvent "
"[[7]](#references).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide utilizes the template with a methanol molecule as the solute, the"
" electronic structure of which is simulated explicitly, and water as the "
"solvent, approximated as a continuous dielectric medium. To account for the "
"[electron correlation "
"effects](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/ijch.202100111) in"
" methanol, while maintaining the balance between the computational cost and "
"accuracy, we only include the $\\sigma$, $\\sigma^{*}$, and lone pair "
"orbitals in the active space simulated with SQD IEF-PCM. This orbital "
"selection is done with [atomic valence active space (AVAS) "
"method](https://github.com/pyscf/pyscf.github.io/blob/master/examples/mcscf/43-avas.py)"
" using the C[2s,2p], O[2s,2p], and H[1s] atomic orbital components, which "
"results in the active space of 14 electrons and 12 orbitals (14e,12o). The "
"reference orbitals are calculated with closed-shell Hartree Fock using the "
"cc-pvdz basis set.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang gabay na ito ay gumagamit ng template na may methanol molecule bilang "
"solute, kung saan ang electronic structure ay sini-simulate nang tahasan, at"
" tubig bilang solvent, na naka-approximate bilang isang tuloy-tuloy na "
"dielectric medium. Upang isaalang-alang ang [electron correlation "
"effects](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1002/ijch.202100111) sa"
" methanol, habang pinapanatili ang balanse sa pagitan ng computational cost "
"at accuracy, isinama lamang namin ang $\\sigma$, $\\sigma^{*}$, at lone pair"
" orbitals sa active space na sini-simulate gamit ang SQD IEF-PCM. Ang "
"orbital selection na ito ay ginagawa gamit ang [atomic valence active space "
"(AVAS) "
"method](https://github.com/pyscf/pyscf.github.io/blob/master/examples/mcscf/43-avas.py)"
" gamit ang C[2s,2p], O[2s,2p], at H[1s] atomic orbital components, na nagre-"
"resulta sa active space na 14 electrons at 12 orbitals (14e,12o). Ang "
"reference orbitals ay kinakalkula gamit ang closed-shell Hartree Fock na may"
" cc-pvdz basis set.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow introduction {#workflow-introduction}"
msgstr "Panimula sa workflow {#workflow-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This interactive guide shows how to upload this function template to Qiskit "
"Serverless and run an example workload. The template is structured as a "
"Qiskit pattern with four steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang interactive na gabay na ito ay nagpapakita kung paano i-upload ang "
"function template na ito sa Qiskit Serverless at magpatakbo ng halimbawang "
"workload. Ang template ay nakabalangkas bilang isang Qiskit pattern na may "
"apat na hakbang:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Collect input and map the problem {#1-collect-input-and-map-the-problem}"
msgstr ""
"1. Kolektahin ang input at i-map ang problema {#1-collect-input-and-map-the-"
"problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This step takes the geometry of the molecule, selected active space, "
"solvation model, LUCJ options, and SQD options as an input. It then produces"
" the PySCF Checkpoint file, which contains the Hartree-Fock (HF) IEF-PCM "
"data. This data will be used in the SQD portion of the workflow. For the "
"LUCJ portion of the workflow, the input section also generates the gas-phase"
" HF data, which is stored internally in PySCF FCIDUMP format.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kinukuha ng hakbang na ito ang geometry ng molecule, napiling active space, "
"solvation model, LUCJ options, at SQD options bilang input. Pagkatapos ay "
"gumagawa ito ng PySCF Checkpoint file, na naglalaman ng Hartree-Fock (HF) "
"IEF-PCM data. Ang data na ito ay gagamitin sa SQD na bahagi ng workflow. "
"Para sa LUCJ na bahagi ng workflow, gumagawa rin ang input section ng gas-"
"phase HF data, na iniimbak nang internal sa PySCF FCIDUMP format.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The information from the HF gas-phase simulation and the definition of the "
"active space are taken as input. Importantly, it also uses the user-defined "
"information from the input section concerning the error suppression, number "
"of shots, circuit transpiler optimization level, and the qubit layout.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang impormasyon mula sa HF gas-phase simulation at ang kahulugan ng active "
"space ay kinukuha bilang input. Mahalaga, gumagamit din ito ng impormasyong "
"tinukoy ng user mula sa input section tungkol sa error suppression, bilang "
"ng shots, circuit transpiler optimization level, at qubit layout.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It generates one-electron and two-electron integrals within the defined "
"active space. The integrals are then used to perform classical CCSD "
"calculations, which return t2 amplitudes that we use to parametrize the LUCJ"
" circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagawa ito ng one-electron at two-electron integrals sa loob ng tinukoy na"
" active space. Ang mga integrals ay ginagamit pagkatapos upang magsagawa ng "
"classical CCSD calculations, na nagbabalik ng t2 amplitudes na ginagamit "
"natin upang i-parametrize ang LUCJ circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Optimize the circuit {#2-optimize-the-circuit}"
msgstr "2. I-optimize ang circuit {#2-optimize-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LUCJ circuit is then transpiled into an ISA circuit for the target "
"hardware. A Sampler primitive is then instantiated with a default set of "
"error mitigation options to manage the execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ini-transpile ang LUCJ circuit tungo sa isang ISA circuit para "
"sa target hardware. Susunod, ini-instantiate ang isang Sampler primitive na "
"may default na set ng error mitigation options upang pamahalaan ang "
"execution.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Execute the circuit {#3-execute-the-circuit}"
msgstr "3. I-execute ang circuit {#3-execute-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LUCJ calculations return the bitstrings for each measurement, where "
"these bitstrings correspond to electron configurations of the studied "
"system. The bitstrings are then used as input for post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang LUCJ calculations ay nagbabalik ng mga bitstrings para sa bawat "
"measurement, kung saan ang mga bitstrings na ito ay tumutugma sa electron "
"configurations ng pinag-aaralang system. Ginagamit pagkatapos ang mga "
"bitstrings bilang input para sa post-processing.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Post-process by using SQD {#4-post-process-by-using-sqd}"
msgstr "4. I-post-process gamit ang SQD {#4-post-process-by-using-sqd}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This final step takes the PySCF Checkpoint file containing the HF IEF-PCM "
"information, the bitstrings representing the electron configurations "
"predicted by LUCJ, and the user-defined SQD options selected in the input "
"section as input. As  output, it produces the SQD IEF-PCM total energy of "
"the lowest energy batch and the corresponding solvation free energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling hakbang na ito ay kumukuha ng PySCF Checkpoint file na naglalaman"
" ng HF IEF-PCM information, ang mga bitstrings na kumakatawan sa electron "
"configurations na hinulaan ng LUCJ, at ang user-defined na SQD options na "
"pinili sa input section bilang input. Bilang output, gumagawa ito ng SQD "
"IEF-PCM total energy ng pinakamababang energy batch at ang kaukulang "
"solvation free energy.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Options {#options}"
msgstr "Mga opsyon {#options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this template you must specify options for generating the LUCJ circuit, "
"and SQD run parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa template na ito kailangan mong tukuyin ang mga opsyon para sa pagbuo"
" ng LUCJ circuit, at mga SQD run parameter.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "LUCJ options {#lucj-options}"
msgstr "Mga LUCJ option {#lucj-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the LUCJ quantum circuit is executed, a set of samples that represent "
"the computational basis states from the probability distribution of the "
"molecular system are produced. To balance the depth of the LUCJ circuit and "
"its expressibility, the qubits corresponding to the spin orbitals with the "
"opposite spin have the two-qubit gates applied between them when these "
"qubits are neighbors through a single ancilla qubit. To implement this "
"approach on IBM hardware with a heavy-hex topology, qubits that represent "
"the spin orbitals with the same spin are connected through a line topology "
"where each line takes a zig-zag shape due to the heavy-hex connectivity of "
"the target hardware, while the qubits that represent the spin orbitals with "
"the opposite spin only have a connection at every fourth qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag ang LUCJ quantum circuit ay ine-execute, isang set ng mga sample na "
"kumakatawan sa computational basis states mula sa probability distribution "
"ng molecular system ang nalilikha. Upang balansehin ang lalim ng LUCJ "
"circuit at ang expressibility nito, ang mga qubits na tumutugma sa spin "
"orbitals na may magkasalungat na spin ay may dalawang-qubit gates na "
"inilalapat sa pagitan nila kapag ang mga qubits na ito ay magkalapit sa "
"pamamagitan ng isang ancilla qubit. Upang ipatupad ang pamamaraang ito sa "
"IBM hardware na may heavy-hex topology, ang mga qubits na kumakatawan sa "
"spin orbitals na may parehong spin ay konektado sa pamamagitan ng isang line"
" topology kung saan ang bawat linya ay nag-zigzag dahil sa heavy-hex "
"connectivity ng target hardware, habang ang mga qubits na kumakatawan sa "
"spin orbitals na may magkasalungat na spin ay may koneksyon lamang sa bawat "
"ikaapat na qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more details on the required options:\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more details on the required options:\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The user has to provide the `initial_layout` array corresponding to the "
"qubits that satisfy this [_zig-zag_ "
"pattern](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2023/sc/d3sc02516k) in "
"the `lucj_options` section of the SQD IEF-PCM function. In case of SQD IEF-"
"PCM (14e,12o)/cc-pvdz simulations of methanol, we chose the initial qubit "
"layout corresponding to the main diagonal of the Eagle R3 QPU. Here, the "
"first 12 elements of the `initial_layout` array `[0, 14, 18, 19, 20, 33, 39,"
" 40, 41, 53, 60, 61, ...]` correspond to the alpha spin orbitals. The last "
"12 elements `[... 2, 3, 4, 15, 22, 23, 24, 34, 43, 44, 45, 54]` correspond "
"to beta spin orbitals.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangang ibigay ng user ang `initial_layout` array na tumutugma sa mga "
"qubits na tumutugon sa [_zig-zag_ "
"pattern](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2023/sc/d3sc02516k) na "
"ito sa `lucj_options` section ng SQD IEF-PCM function. Sa kaso ng SQD IEF-"
"PCM (14e,12o)/cc-pvdz simulations ng methanol, pinili namin ang initial "
"qubit layout na tumutugma sa pangunahing diagonal ng Eagle R3 QPU. Dito, ang"
" unang 12 elemento ng `initial_layout` array `[0, 14, 18, 19, 20, 33, 39, "
"40, 41, 53, 60, 61, ...]` ay tumutugma sa alpha spin orbitals. Ang huling 12"
" elemento `[... 2, 3, 4, 15, 22, 23, 24, 34, 43, 44, 45, 54]` ay tumutugma "
"sa beta spin orbitals.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Importantly, the user has to determine the `number_of_shots`, which "
"corresponds to the number of measurements in the LUCJ circuit. The number of"
" shots needs to be sufficiently large because the first step of S-CORE "
"procedure relies on the samples in the right particle sector to obtain the "
"initial approximation to the ground-state occupation number distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalaga, kailangang matukoy ng user ang `number_of_shots`, na tumutugma sa "
"bilang ng mga measurement sa LUCJ circuit. Kailangang sapat na malaki ang "
"bilang ng shots dahil ang unang hakbang ng S-CORE procedure ay umaasa sa mga"
" sample sa tamang particle sector upang makuha ang paunang approximation sa "
"ground-state occupation number distribution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The number of shots is highly system- and hardware-dependent, but [non-"
"covalent](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.09209), [fragment-"
"based](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.09861), and [implicit "
"solvent](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030) SQD studies "
"suggest that one can reach the chemical accuracy by following these "
"guidelines:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bilang ng shots ay lubhang system- at hardware-dependent, ngunit ang "
"[non-covalent](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.09209), [fragment-"
"based](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.09861), at [implicit "
"solvent](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030) na SQD na pag-"
"aaral ay nagmumungkahi na maaaring maabot ang chemical accuracy sa "
"pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa mga gabay na ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"20,000 - 200,000 shots for systems with fewer than 16 molecular orbitals (32"
" spin orbitals)\n"
msgstr ""
"20,000 - 200,000 shots para sa mga system na may mas kaunti sa 16 molecular "
"orbitals (32 spin orbitals)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "200,000 shots for systems with 16 - 18 molecular orbitals\n"
msgstr "200,000 shots para sa mga system na may 16 - 18 molecular orbitals\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"200,000 - 2,000,000 shots for systems with more than 18 molecular orbitals\n"
msgstr ""
"200,000 - 2,000,000 shots para sa mga system na may higit sa 18 molecular "
"orbitals\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The required number of shots is affected by the number of spin orbitals in "
"the studied system and by the size of the Hilbert space corresponding to the"
" selected active space within the studied system. Generally, instances with "
"smaller Hilbert spaces require fewer shots. Other available LUCJ options are"
" [circuit transpiler optimization "
"level](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/guides/set-optimization) and [error "
"suppression options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/guides/error-mitigation-"
"and-suppression-techniques). Note that these options also affect the "
"required number of shots and the resulting accuracy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kinakailangang bilang ng shots ay apektado ng bilang ng spin orbitals sa"
" pinag-aaralang system at ng laki ng Hilbert space na tumutugma sa napiling "
"active space sa loob ng pinag-aaralang system. Sa pangkalahatan, ang mga "
"instance na may mas maliliit na Hilbert spaces ay nangangailangan ng mas "
"kaunting shots. Ang iba pang available na LUCJ options ay [circuit "
"transpiler optimization level](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/guides/set-"
"optimization) at [error suppression "
"options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques). Tandaan na ang mga opsyong ito ay nakakaapekto rin "
"sa kinakailangang bilang ng shots at sa resultang accuracy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SQD options {#sqd-options}"
msgstr "Mga SQD option {#sqd-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Important options in SQD simulations include the `sqd_iterations`, "
"`number_of_batches`, and `samples_per_batch`. Generally, the lower number of"
" samples per batch can be counteracted with more batches "
"(`number_of_batches`) and more iterations of S-CORE (`sqd_iterations`). With"
" more batches we can sample more variations of the configurational "
"subspaces. Since the lowest-energy batch is taken as the solution for the "
"ground state energy of the system, more batches can improve the results "
"through better statistics. Additional iterations of S-CORE allow more "
"configurations to be recovered from the original LUCJ distribution if the "
"number of samples in the correct particle sector is low. This can allow the "
"number of samples per batch to be reduced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mahahalagang opsyon sa SQD simulations ay kinabibilangan ng "
"`sqd_iterations`, `number_of_batches`, at `samples_per_batch`. Sa "
"pangkalahatan, ang mas mababang bilang ng samples per batch ay maaaring "
"kontrahin ng mas maraming batches (`number_of_batches`) at mas maraming "
"iterations ng S-CORE (`sqd_iterations`). Sa mas maraming batches maaari "
"nating ma-sample ang mas maraming variasyon ng configurational subspaces. "
"Dahil ang pinakamababang-energy batch ang kinukuha bilang solusyon para sa "
"ground state energy ng system, ang mas maraming batches ay maaaring mapabuti"
" ang mga resulta sa pamamagitan ng mas magandang statistics. Ang mga "
"karagdagang iteration ng S-CORE ay nagbibigay-daan sa mas maraming "
"configuration na ma-recover mula sa orihinal na LUCJ distribution kung ang "
"bilang ng mga sample sa tamang particle sector ay mababa. Ito ay maaaring "
"magpahintulot na mabawasan ang bilang ng samples per batch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more information about configuring the SQD options:\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Click to expand for more information about configuring the SQD options:\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative strategy is to use more samples per batch, which ensures that"
" most of the initial LUCJ samples in right particle space are used during "
"the S-CORE procedure, and individual subspaces encapsulate a sufficient "
"variety of electron configurations. In turn, this reduces the number of "
"required S-CORE steps, where only two or three iterations of SQD are needed "
"if the number of samples per batch is large enough. However, more samples "
"per batch results in a higher computational cost of each diagonalization "
"step. Hence, the balance between the accuracy and computational cost in SQD "
"simulations can be achieved by choosing  `sqd_iterations`, "
"`number_of_batches`, and `samples_per_batch` optimally.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang alternatibong estratehiya ay ang gumamit ng mas maraming samples "
"per batch, na tumitiyak na karamihan sa mga paunang LUCJ sample sa tamang "
"particle space ay ginagamit sa panahon ng S-CORE procedure, at ang mga "
"indibidwal na subspace ay naglalaman ng sapat na iba't ibang electron "
"configurations. Dahil dito, nababawasan ang bilang ng kinakailangang S-CORE "
"steps, kung saan dalawa o tatlong iteration lamang ng SQD ang kailangan kung"
" sapat na malaki ang bilang ng samples per batch. Gayunpaman, ang mas "
"maraming samples per batch ay nagre-resulta sa mas mataas na computational "
"cost ng bawat diagonalization step. Kaya, ang balanse sa pagitan ng accuracy"
" at computational cost sa SQD simulations ay maaaring makamit sa pamamagitan"
" ng pagpili ng `sqd_iterations`, `number_of_batches`, at `samples_per_batch`"
" nang optimal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [SQD IEF-PCM study](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030) "
"shows that when three iterations of S-CORE are used, the chemical accuracy "
"can be reached by following these guidelines:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [SQD IEF-PCM study](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030) "
"ay nagpapakita na kapag tatlong iteration ng S-CORE ang ginamit, ang "
"chemical accuracy ay maaaring maabot sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa mga gabay"
" na ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "600 samples per batch in methanol SQD IEF-PCM (14e,12o) simulations\n"
msgstr "600 samples per batch sa methanol SQD IEF-PCM (14e,12o) simulations\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1500 samples per batch in methylamine SQD IEF-PCM (14e,13o) simulations\n"
msgstr ""
"1500 samples per batch sa methylamine SQD IEF-PCM (14e,13o) simulations\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6000 samples per batch in water SQD IEF-PCM (8e,23o) simulations\n"
msgstr "6000 samples per batch sa water SQD IEF-PCM (8e,23o) simulations\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "16000 samples per batch in ethanol SQD IEF-PCM (20e,18o) simulations\n"
msgstr "16000 samples per batch sa ethanol SQD IEF-PCM (20e,18o) simulations\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Just like the required number of shots in LUCJ, the required number of "
"samples per batch used in S-CORE procedure is highly system- and hardware-"
"dependent. The examples above can be used to estimate the initial point for "
"the benchmark of required number of samples per batch. The tutorial on "
"systematic benchmark of the required number of samples per batch can be "
"found [here](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"sqd/how_tos/choose_subspace_dimension.html).\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng kinakailangang bilang ng shots sa LUCJ, ang kinakailangang bilang "
"ng samples per batch na ginagamit sa S-CORE procedure ay lubhang system- at "
"hardware-dependent. Ang mga halimbawa sa itaas ay maaaring gamitin upang "
"tantiyahin ang panimulang punto para sa benchmark ng kinakailangang bilang "
"ng samples per batch. Ang tutorial sa sistematikong benchmark ng "
"kinakailangang bilang ng samples per batch ay matatagpuan "
"[dito](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"sqd/how_tos/choose_subspace_dimension.html).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deploy and execute the template SQD IEF-PCM function {#deploy-and-execute-"
"the-template-sqd-ief-pcm-function}"
msgstr ""
"I-deploy at i-execute ang template SQD IEF-PCM function {#deploy-and-"
"execute-the-template-sqd-ief-pcm-function}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication {#authentication}"
msgstr "Authentication {#authentication}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use `qiskit-ibm-catalog` to authenticate to `QiskitServerless` with your API"
" key (token), which can be found on the [IBM Quantum "
"Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) dashboard. This allows for the "
"instantiation of the serverless client to upload or run the selected "
"function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang `qiskit-ibm-catalog` upang mag-authenticate sa "
"`QiskitServerless` gamit ang iyong API key (token), na matatagpuan sa [IBM "
"Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) dashboard. Nagbibigay-daan "
"ito sa pag-instantiate ng serverless client upang mag-upload o magpatakbo ng"
" napiling function:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, use `save_account()` to save your credentials in a local "
"environment (see the [Set up your IBM Cloud account](/guides/cloud-"
"setup#cloud-save) guide). Note that this writes your credentials to the same"
" file as "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#save_account):\n"
msgstr ""
"Opsyonal, gamitin ang `save_account()` upang i-save ang iyong mga credential"
" sa isang lokal na environment (tingnan ang gabay na [I-set up ang iyong IBM"
" Cloud account](/guides/cloud-setup#cloud-save)). Tandaan na isinusulat nito"
" ang iyong mga credential sa parehong file tulad ng "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#save_account):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the [account is saved](/guides/save-credentials), there is no need to "
"provide the token to authenticate:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang [account ay naka-save na](/guides/save-credentials), hindi na "
"kailangang ibigay ang token upang mag-authenticate:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the template {#upload-the-template}"
msgstr "I-upload ang template {#upload-the-template}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To upload a custom Qiskit Function, you must first instantiate a "
"`QiskitFunction` object that defines the function source code. The title "
"will allow you to identify the function once it's in the remote cluster. The"
" main entry point is the file that contains `if __name__ == \"__main__\"`. "
"If your workflow requires additional source files, you can define a working "
"directory that will be uploaded together with the entry point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang mag-upload ng custom na Qiskit Function, kailangan mo munang mag-"
"instantiate ng isang `QiskitFunction` object na tumutukoy sa function source"
" code. Ang pamagat ay magbibigay-daan sa iyo na tukuyin ang function kapag "
"nasa remote cluster na ito. Ang pangunahing entry point ay ang file na "
"naglalaman ng `if __name__ == \"__main__\"`. Kung ang iyong workflow ay "
"nangangailangan ng mga karagdagang source file, maaari kang tumukoy ng isang"
" working directory na ia-upload kasama ang entry point.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Once the instance is ready, upload it to serverless:\n"
msgstr "Kapag handa na ang instance, i-upload ito sa serverless:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To check if the program successfully uploaded, use `serverless.list()`:\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang suriin kung matagumpay na na-upload ang program, gamitin ang "
"`serverless.list()`:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Load and run the template remotely {#load-and-run-the-template-remotely}"
msgstr ""
"I-load at patakbuhin ang template nang remote {#load-and-run-the-template-"
"remotely}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The function template has been uploaded, so you can run it remotely with "
"Qiskit Serverless. First, load the template by name:\n"
msgstr ""
"Na-upload na ang function template, kaya maaari mo na itong patakbuhin nang "
"remote gamit ang Qiskit Serverless. Una, i-load ang template ayon sa "
"pangalan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, run the template with the domain-level inputs for SQD-IEF PCM. This "
"example specifies a methanol-based workload.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, patakbuhin ang template gamit ang domain-level inputs para sa SQD-"
"IEF PCM. Ang halimbawang ito ay tumutukoy sa isang methanol-based "
"workload.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check the detailed status of the job:\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang detalyadong status ng job:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the job is running, you can fetch logs created from the `logger.info` "
"outputs. These can provide actionable information about the progress of the "
"SQD IEF-PCM workflow. For example, the same spin orbital connections, or the"
" two-qubit depth of the final ISA circuit intended for execution on "
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang tumatakbo ang job, maaari kang kumuha ng mga log na ginawa mula sa "
"`logger.info` outputs. Maaaring magbigay ang mga ito ng naaaksyunang "
"impormasyon tungkol sa progreso ng SQD IEF-PCM workflow. Halimbawa, ang "
"parehong spin orbital connections, o ang two-qubit depth ng huling ISA "
"circuit na nilalayong i-execute sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calling for the job result blocks the rest of the program until a result is "
"available. After the job is done, you can retrieve the results. These "
"include the solvation free energy, as well as information about the lowest "
"energy batch, lowest energy value, and other useful information such as the "
"total solver duration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hinaharangan ng pagtawag sa job result ang natitirang bahagi ng program "
"hanggang may available na resulta. Pagkatapos matapos ang job, maaari mong "
"kunin ang mga resulta. Kasama dito ang solvation free energy, pati na rin "
"ang impormasyon tungkol sa pinakamababang energy batch, pinakamababang "
"halaga ng energy, at iba pang kapaki-pakinabang na impormasyon tulad ng "
"kabuuang tagal ng solver.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the result metadata includes a resource usage summary that lets you better estimate the QPU and CPU time required for each workload (this example ran on a dummy device, so actual resource usage times might differ).\n"
"After the job completes, the entire logging output will be available.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang result metadata ay nagsasama ng resource usage summary na nagbibigay-daan sa iyo na mas mahusay na tantyahin ang QPU at CPU time na kinakailangan para sa bawat workload (ang halimbawang ito ay tumakbo sa isang dummy device, kaya ang aktwal na resource usage times ay maaaring mag-iba).\n"
"Pagkatapos makumpleto ang job, ang buong logging output ay magiging available.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"info\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"info\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Review the guide on building a function template for [Hamiltonian "
"simulation](/guides/function-template-hamiltonian-simulation)\n"
msgstr ""
"Suriin ang gabay sa pagbuo ng function template para sa [Hamiltonian "
"simulation](/guides/function-template-hamiltonian-simulation)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check out the source files for this template on "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-"
"templates/tree/main/chemistry/sqd_pcm)\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang mga source file para sa template na ito sa "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-"
"templates/tree/main/chemistry/sqd_pcm)\n"

